IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 12 Division 1, second half, and Division 3: security for costs and costs (s 388), a witness's solicitor
-- (s 389), disposal of the shares of a shareholder who cannot be found (s 390), relief for officers, auditors and experts (s 391),
-- irregularities (s 392), production of books where an offence is suspected (s 394), the Court's power to compel compliance (s 399),
-- injunctions (s 409A) and the appeal from the Registrar (s 409C). Part agent sgo.
--
-- The grant rule and the periods ruling, as this module reads them (NOTES.md, fork register and split sites):
--   * a "may" whose gate is "if", "on application" or "with ...": a failed gate answers NOTHING (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1);
--   * a "may" whose gate is "where", "when" or "upon": a failed gate answers JUST FALSE (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)), listed as a
--     split site of type (ii), the other reading being NOTHING;
--   * a bar written "is not to ... unless": JUST FALSE where the "unless" is not met.

§ `Section 388: security for costs, and costs`

-- src:27378 | 388.—(1) Where a corporation is claimant in any action or other
-- src:27379 | legal proceeding the court having jurisdiction in the matter may, if it
-- src:27380 | appears by credible testimony that there is reason to believe that the
-- src:27381 | corporation will be unable to pay the costs of the defendant if
-- src:27382 | successful in the defendant’s defence, require sufficient security to be
-- src:27387 | given for those costs and stay all proceedings until the security is
-- src:27388 | given.
@ref s 388(1) (src:27378-27388)
GIVEN `the corporation is claimant in an action or other legal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears by credible testimony that there is reason to believe that the corporation will be unable to pay the costs of the defendant if successful in the defendant's defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(1) the court may require sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant` MEANS
    IF NOT `the corporation is claimant in an action or other legal proceeding`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a corporation is claimant in any action or other legal proceeding" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-388-1
    ELSE (IF `it appears by credible testimony that there is reason to believe that the corporation will be unable to pay the costs of the defendant if successful in the defendant's defence`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court having jurisdiction in the matter may, if it appears by credible testimony that there is reason to believe ..." is an "if" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

-- "and stay all proceedings until the security is given": a bar that lasts until the security is given (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d): JUST TRUE before X, JUST FALSE after X).
@ref s 388(1) (src:27378-27388)
GIVEN `the court has required sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(1) the proceedings are stayed until the security is given` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court has required sufficient security to be given for the costs of the defendant`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the stay is one the court may order "and" together with the requirement
    ELSE (IF `the security has been given`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "stay all proceedings until the security is given"; once it is given the stay ends
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:27394 | (2) The costs of any proceeding before a court under this Act must
-- src:27395 | be borne by such party to the proceeding as the court may, in its
-- src:27396 | discretion, direct.
@ref s 388(2) (src:27394-27396)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a proceeding before a court under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has directed, in its discretion, that the party bears the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(2) the party must bear the costs of the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is a proceeding before a court under this Act` AND `the court has directed, in its discretion, that the party bears the costs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "must be borne by such party to the proceeding as the court may, in its discretion, direct" leaves the party to the court's direction, which is a judgment handed to the court

§ `Section 389: a witness's right to a solicitor`

DECLARE `s 389 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 389 employ a solicitor at the person's own cost`

-- src:27400 | 389. Any person summoned for examination under Part 9 may, at
-- src:27401 | the person’s own cost, employ a solicitor who is at liberty to put to the
-- src:27402 | person such questions as the inspector, Court or District Judge
-- src:27403 | considers just for the purpose of enabling the person to explain or
-- src:27404 | qualify any answers given by the person.
@ref s 389 (src:27400-27404)
GIVEN `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389 the person may employ a solicitor at the person's own cost` MEANS
    IF `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person summoned for examination under Part 9"

@ref s 389 (src:27400-27404)
GIVEN `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspector, Court or District Judge considers the question just for the purpose of enabling the person to explain or qualify any answers given by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 389 the solicitor is at liberty to put the question to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has been summoned for examination under Part 9` AND `the inspector, Court or District Judge considers the question just for the purpose of enabling the person to explain or qualify any answers given by the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such questions as the inspector, Court or District Judge considers just"; the judgment is the inspector's, the Court's or the District Judge's, taken here as an input

@ref s 389 (src:27400-27404)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 389 act`
`s 389 a person summoned for examination under Part 9 may employ a solicitor` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MAY `s 389 employ a solicitor at the person's own cost`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 390: disposal of the shares of a shareholder whose whereabouts are unknown`

DECLARE `s 390 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 390(1) cause an advertisement to be published in a newspaper`
    `s 390(2) transfer the shares held by the shareholder to the Official Receiver`
    `s 390(3) sell or dispose of the shares received and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`

-- "for a period of not less than 10 years": a whole number of years, at least 10.
-- src:27410 | 390.—(1) Where by the exercise of reasonable diligence a
-- src:27411 | company is unable to discover the whereabouts of a shareholder
-- src:27412 | for a period of not less than 10 years, the company may cause an
-- src:27413 | advertisement to be published in a newspaper circulating in the place
-- src:27414 | shown in the register of members as the address of the shareholder
-- src:27415 | stating that the company after the expiration of one month from the
-- src:27416 | date of the advertisement intends to transfer the shares to the Official
-- src:27417 | Receiver.
@ref s 390(1) (src:27410-27417)
GIVEN `the company is unable by the exercise of reasonable diligence to discover the whereabouts of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of years for which the company has been unable to discover the whereabouts of the shareholder` IS A NUMBER
      `the advertisement is published in a newspaper circulating in the place shown in the register of members as the address of the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the advertisement states that the company after the expiration of one month from the date of the advertisement intends to transfer the shares to the Official Receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(1) the company may cause the advertisement to be published` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is unable by the exercise of reasonable diligence to discover the whereabouts of a shareholder` AND `the number of years for which the company has been unable to discover the whereabouts of the shareholder` AT LEAST 10)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where by the exercise of reasonable diligence a company is unable to discover the whereabouts of a shareholder for a period of not less than 10 years" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (a) and (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-390-1
    ELSE (IF    `the advertisement is published in a newspaper circulating in the place shown in the register of members as the address of the shareholder`
             AND `the advertisement states that the company after the expiration of one month from the date of the advertisement intends to transfer the shares to the Official Receiver`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may cause an advertisement to be published in a newspaper circulating in the place shown ... stating that the company after the expiration of one month ... intends to transfer the shares"

@ref s 390(1) (src:27410-27417)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 390 act`
`s 390(1) a company that cannot find a shareholder may cause the advertisement to be published` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MAY `s 390(1) cause an advertisement to be published in a newspaper`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- "If, after the expiration of one month from the date of the advertisement, the whereabouts of the shareholder remain unknown, the company may transfer the shares ...
-- and for that purpose may execute for and on behalf of the owner a transfer of those shares to the Official Receiver." One month from the date: sg-periods P1, P4;
-- "after the expiration" is the day after the last day of the month.
-- src:27419 | (2) If, after the expiration of one month from the date of the
-- src:27420 | advertisement, the whereabouts of the shareholder remain unknown,
-- src:27421 | the company may transfer the shares held by the shareholder in the
-- src:27422 | company to the Official Receiver and for that purpose may execute
-- src:27423 | for and on behalf of the owner a transfer of those shares to the Official
-- src:27424 | Receiver.
@ref s 390(2) (src:27419-27424)
GIVEN `the date of the advertisement` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company transfers the shares` IS A DATE
      `the whereabouts of the shareholder remain unknown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(2) the company may transfer the shares held by the shareholder to the Official Receiver and execute the transfer for the owner` MEANS
    IF `the whereabouts of the shareholder remain unknown` AND `the day on which the company transfers the shares` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the advertisement` 1 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, after the expiration of one month from the date of the advertisement, the whereabouts of the shareholder remain unknown, the company may transfer" is an "if" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

@ref s 390(2) (src:27419-27424)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 390 act`
`s 390(2) a company that still cannot find the shareholder may transfer the shares to the Official Receiver` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MAY `s 390(2) transfer the shares held by the shareholder to the Official Receiver`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:27426 | (3) The Official Receiver must sell or dispose of any shares so
-- src:27427 | received in such manner and at such time as the Official Receiver
-- src:27428 | thinks fit and must deal with proceeds of the sale or disposal as if they
-- src:27429 | were moneys paid to the Official Receiver pursuant to section 197 of
-- src:27430 | the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 390(3) (src:27426-27430)
GIVEN `the Official Receiver has received shares transferred under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(3) the Official Receiver must sell or dispose of the shares and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` MEANS
    IF `the Official Receiver has received shares transferred under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any shares so received"

@ref s 390(3) (src:27426-27430)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 390 act`
`s 390(3) the Official Receiver must sell or dispose of the shares received` MEANS
    PARTY `Official Receiver`
    MUST `s 390(3) sell or dispose of the shares received and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 391: power to grant relief`

§§ `Section 391(3): the persons to whom the section applies`

-- The list is "The persons to whom this section applies are (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." with no "only": read as not closed (fork F-391-3).
-- src:27462 | (3) The persons to whom this section applies are —
-- src:27464 | (a) officers of a corporation;
-- src:27466 | (b) persons employed by a corporation as auditors, whether
-- src:27467 | they are or are not officers of the corporation;
-- src:27469 | (c) experts within the meaning of this Act; and
-- src:27471 | (d) persons who are receivers, receivers and managers or
-- src:27472 | liquidators appointed or directed by the Court to carry out
-- src:27473 | any duty under this Act in relation to a corporation and all
-- src:27474 | other persons so appointed or so directed.
@ref s 391(3) (src:27462-27474)
GIVEN position IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is`
      `the person is employed by a corporation as auditor, whether or not the person is an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an engineer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a valuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is another whose profession or reputation gives authority to a statement made by him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a receiver, receiver and manager or liquidator appointed or directed by the Court to carry out a duty under this Act in relation to a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is another person so appointed or so directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 391(3) the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` MEANS
    IF    `s 4(1) "officer" the person is an officer of the corporation` position EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the person is employed by a corporation as auditor, whether or not the person is an officer of the corporation`
       OR `s 4(1) "expert" the person is within the word expert` `the person is an engineer` `the person is a valuer` `the person is an accountant` `the person is another whose profession or reputation gives authority to a statement made by him or her` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the person is a receiver, receiver and manager or liquidator appointed or directed by the Court to carry out a duty under this Act in relation to a corporation`
       OR `the person is another person so appointed or so directed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The persons to whom this section applies are (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." lists four heads and does not say "only"

§§ `Section 391(1), (1A) and (2): relief`

-- src:27439 | 391.—(1) If in any proceedings for negligence, default, breach of
-- src:27440 | duty or breach of trust against a person to whom this section applies,
-- src:27441 | it appears to the court before which the proceedings are taken that the
-- src:27442 | person is or may be liable in respect thereof but that the person has
-- src:27443 | acted honestly and reasonably and that, having regard to all the
-- src:27444 | circumstances of the case including those connected with the person’s
-- src:27445 | appointment, the person ought fairly to be excused for the negligence,
-- src:27446 | default or breach, the court may relieve the person either wholly or
-- src:27447 | partly from the person’s liability on such terms as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 391(1) (src:27439-27447)
GIVEN `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the person is or may be liable in respect of the negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
      `having regard to all the circumstances of the case including those connected with the person's appointment, the person ought fairly to be excused for the negligence, default or breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 391(1) the court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from the person's liability` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies`
       AND `the proceedings are proceedings for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust against the person`
       AND `it appears to the court that the person is or may be liable in respect of the negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust`
       AND `the person has acted honestly and reasonably`
       AND `having regard to all the circumstances of the case including those connected with the person's appointment, the person ought fairly to be excused for the negligence, default or breach`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in any proceedings ... it appears to the court ... the court may relieve" is an "if" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-391-1); "ought fairly to be excused" is the court's judgment, taken here as an input

-- src:27449 | (1A) To avoid doubt and without limiting subsection (1), “liability”
-- src:27450 | includes the liability of a person to whom this section applies to
-- src:27451 | account for profits made or received.
@ref s 391(1A) (src:27449-27451)
GIVEN `the liability is a liability of a person to whom section 391 applies to account for profits made or received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 391(1A) the liability is within the word liability in section 391(1)` MEANS
    IF `the liability is a liability of a person to whom section 391 applies to account for profits made or received`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "\"liability\" includes the liability of a person to whom this section applies to account for profits made or received"

-- src:27453 | (2) Where any person to whom this section applies has reason to
-- src:27454 | apprehend that any claim will or might be made against the person in
-- src:27455 | respect of any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust
-- src:27456 | the person may apply to the Court for relief, and the Court has the
-- src:27457 | same power to relieve the person as under this section it would have
-- src:27458 | had if it had been a court before which proceedings against the person
-- src:27459 | for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust had been
-- src:27460 | brought.
@ref s 391(2) (src:27453-27460)
GIVEN `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against the person in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 391(2) the person may apply to the Court for relief` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person to whom section 391 applies` AND `the person has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against the person in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any person to whom this section applies has reason to apprehend that any claim will or might be made ... the person may apply to the Court" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-391-2

§ `Section 392: irregularities`

DECLARE `s 392(4) kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `s 392(4)(a) an order declaring that an act, matter, thing or proceeding is not invalid by reason of a contravention or failure to comply`
    `s 392(4)(b) an order directing the rectification of a register kept by the Registrar`
    `s 392(4)(c) an order relieving a person from civil liability in respect of a contravention or failure`
    `s 392(4)(d) an order extending or abridging the period for doing an act or taking a proceeding`
    `s 392(4) a consequential or ancillary order`

-- src:27478 | 392.—(1) In this section, unless the contrary intention appears, a
-- src:27479 | reference to a procedural irregularity includes a reference to —
-- src:27484 | (a) the absence of a quorum at a meeting of a corporation, at a
-- src:27485 | meeting of directors or creditors of a corporation or at a
-- src:27486 | joint meeting of creditors and members of a corporation;
-- src:27487 | and
-- src:27489 | (b) a defect, irregularity or deficiency of notice or time.
@ref s 392(1) (src:27478-27489)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in section 392` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the absence of a quorum at a meeting of a corporation, at a meeting of directors or creditors of a corporation or at a joint meeting of creditors and members of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a defect, irregularity or deficiency of notice or time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(1) the matter is within the words procedural irregularity` MEANS
    IF `a contrary intention appears in section 392`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, unless the contrary intention appears"
    ELSE (IF `the matter is the absence of a quorum at a meeting of a corporation, at a meeting of directors or creditors of a corporation or at a joint meeting of creditors and members of a corporation` OR `the matter is a defect, irregularity or deficiency of notice or time`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to a procedural irregularity includes a reference to (a) ...; and (b) ..."

-- src:27491 | (2) A proceeding under this Act is not invalidated by reason of any
-- src:27492 | procedural irregularity unless the Court is of the opinion that the
-- src:27493 | irregularity has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot
-- src:27494 | be remedied by any order of the Court and by order declares the
-- src:27495 | proceeding to be invalid.
@ref s 392(2) (src:27491-27495)
GIVEN `the proceeding under this Act is affected by a procedural irregularity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is of the opinion that the irregularity has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court by order declares the proceeding to be invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(2) the proceeding is not invalidated by reason of the procedural irregularity` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceeding under this Act is affected by a procedural irregularity`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A proceeding under this Act is not invalidated by reason of any procedural irregularity"
    ELSE (IF `the Court is of the opinion that the irregularity has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` AND `the Court by order declares the proceeding to be invalid`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not invalidated ... unless the Court is of the opinion that ... and by order declares the proceeding to be invalid"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:27497 | (2A) A meeting to which section 173J(2)(b) or (c) applies is not
-- src:27498 | invalidated by reason of any technological disruption, malfunction or
-- src:27499 | outage unless the Court —
-- src:27501 | (a) is of the opinion that the technological disruption,
-- src:27502 | malfunction or outage has caused or may cause
-- src:27503 | substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any
-- src:27504 | order of the Court; and
-- src:27506 | (b) by order declares the meeting to be invalid.
@ref s 392(2A) (src:27497-27506)
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting to which section 173J(2)(b) or (c) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is affected by technological disruption, malfunction or outage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is of the opinion that the technological disruption, malfunction or outage has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court by order declares the meeting to be invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(2A) the meeting is not invalidated by reason of the technological disruption, malfunction or outage` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the meeting is a meeting to which section 173J(2)(b) or (c) applies` AND `the meeting is affected by technological disruption, malfunction or outage`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A meeting to which section 173J(2)(b) or (c) applies is not invalidated by reason of any technological disruption, malfunction or outage"
    ELSE (IF `the Court is of the opinion that the technological disruption, malfunction or outage has caused or may cause substantial injustice that cannot be remedied by any order of the Court` AND `the Court by order declares the meeting to be invalid`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not invalidated ... unless the Court (a) is of the opinion ...; and (b) by order declares the meeting to be invalid"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:27510 | (3) A meeting held for the purposes of this Act, or a meeting notice
-- src:27511 | of which is required to be given in accordance with the provisions of
-- src:27512 | this Act, or any proceeding at such a meeting, is not invalidated by
-- src:27513 | reason only of the accidental omission to give notice of the meeting or
-- src:27514 | the non‑receipt by any person of notice of the meeting, unless the
-- src:27515 | Court, on the application of the person concerned, a person entitled to
-- src:27516 | attend the meeting or the Registrar, declares proceedings at the
-- src:27517 | meeting to be void.
@ref s 392(3) (src:27510-27517)
GIVEN `the meeting is a meeting held for the purposes of this Act, a meeting notice of which is required to be given in accordance with this Act, or a proceeding at such a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invalidity would arise by reason only of the accidental omission to give notice of the meeting or the non-receipt by any person of notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has declared proceedings at the meeting to be void` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court made the declaration on the application of the person concerned, a person entitled to attend the meeting or the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(3) the meeting or its proceedings are not invalidated by reason only of the omission or non-receipt of notice` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the meeting is a meeting held for the purposes of this Act, a meeting notice of which is required to be given in accordance with this Act, or a proceeding at such a meeting` AND `the invalidity would arise by reason only of the accidental omission to give notice of the meeting or the non-receipt by any person of notice of the meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not invalidated by reason only of the accidental omission to give notice of the meeting or the non-receipt by any person of notice of the meeting"
    ELSE (IF `the Court has declared proceedings at the meeting to be void` AND `the Court made the declaration on the application of the person concerned, a person entitled to attend the meeting or the Registrar`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court, on the application of the person concerned, a person entitled to attend the meeting or the Registrar, declares proceedings at the meeting to be void"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (6): "The Court is not to make an order under this section unless it is satisfied (a) in the case of an order mentioned in subsection (4)(a) (i) ...; (ii) ...; or (iii) ...;
-- (b) in the case of an order mentioned in subsection (4)(c), that the person subject to the civil liability concerned acted honestly; and (c) in every case, that no substantial injustice
-- has been or is likely to be caused to any person." Named as the bar, as the guide asks: JUST TRUE = barred, JUST FALSE = the "unless" is met and this subsection does not bar.
-- src:27559 | (6) The Court is not to make an order under this section unless it is
-- src:27560 | satisfied —
-- src:27562 | (a) in the case of an order mentioned in subsection (4)(a) —
-- src:27564 | (i) that the act, matter or thing, or the proceeding,
-- src:27565 | mentioned in that paragraph is essentially of a
-- src:27566 | procedural nature;
-- src:27568 | (ii) that the person or persons concerned in or party to the
-- src:27569 | contravention or failure acted honestly; or
-- src:27571 | (iii) that it is in the public interest that the order be made;
-- src:27573 | (b) in the case of an order mentioned in subsection (4)(c), that
-- src:27574 | the person subject to the civil liability concerned acted
-- src:27575 | honestly; and
-- src:27580 | (c) in every case, that no substantial injustice has been or is
-- src:27581 | likely to be caused to any person.
@ref s 392(6) (src:27559-27581)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 392(4) kind of order`
      `the act, matter or thing, or the proceeding, is essentially of a procedural nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or persons concerned in or party to the contravention or failure acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the public interest that the order be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person subject to the civil liability concerned acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no substantial injustice has been or is likely to be caused to any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(6) the Court is barred from making the order` MEANS
    IF satisfied THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to make an order under this section unless it is satisfied"; once it is satisfied of every limb that applies, this subsection does not bar
    ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        limbA MEANS `the act, matter or thing, or the proceeding, is essentially of a procedural nature` OR `the person or persons concerned in or party to the contravention or failure acted honestly` OR `it is in the public interest that the order be made`
        every MEANS `no substantial injustice has been or is likely to be caused to any person`
        satisfied MEANS
            CONSIDER kind
            WHEN `s 392(4)(a) an order declaring that an act, matter, thing or proceeding is not invalid by reason of a contravention or failure to comply` THEN limbA AND every
            WHEN `s 392(4)(c) an order relieving a person from civil liability in respect of a contravention or failure` THEN `the person subject to the civil liability concerned acted honestly` AND every
            OTHERWISE every

-- src:27519 | (4) Subject to the following provisions of this section and without
-- src:27520 | limiting any other provision of this Act, the Court may, on application
-- src:27521 | by any interested person, make all or any of the following orders,
-- src:27522 | either unconditionally or subject to such conditions as the Court
-- src:27523 | imposes:
-- src:27525 | (a) an order declaring that any act, matter or thing purporting
-- src:27526 | to have been done, or any proceeding purporting to have
-- src:27527 | been instituted or taken, under this Act or in relation to a
-- src:27532 | corporation is not invalid by reason of any contravention
-- src:27533 | of, or failure to comply with, a provision of this Act or a
-- src:27534 | provision of any of the constituent documents of a
-- src:27535 | corporation;
-- src:27537 | (b) an order directing the rectification of any register kept by
-- src:27538 | the Registrar under this Act;
-- src:27540 | (c) an order relieving a person in whole or in part from any
-- src:27541 | civil liability in respect of a contravention or failure of a
-- src:27542 | kind referred to in paragraph (a);
-- src:27544 | (d) an order extending the period for doing any act, matter or
-- src:27545 | thing or instituting or taking any proceeding under this Act
-- src:27546 | or in relation to a corporation (including an order extending
-- src:27547 | a period where the period concerned expired before the
-- src:27548 | application for the order was made) or abridging the period
-- src:27549 | for doing such an act, matter or thing or instituting or
-- src:27550 | taking such a proceeding,
-- src:27552 | and may make such consequential or ancillary orders as the Court
-- src:27553 | thinks fit.
@ref s 392(4) (src:27519-27553)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 392(4) kind of order`
      `an interested person has applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act, matter or thing, or the proceeding, is essentially of a procedural nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or persons concerned in or party to the contravention or failure acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the public interest that the order be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person subject to the civil liability concerned acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no substantial injustice has been or is likely to be caused to any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(4) the Court may make the order on the application of an interested person` MEANS
    IF NOT `an interested person has applied for the order`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may, on application by any interested person, make all or any of the following orders" is an "on application" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1; split site type (ii), fork F-392-4)
    ELSE (IF `s 392(6) the Court is barred from making the order` kind `the act, matter or thing, or the proceeding, is essentially of a procedural nature` `the person or persons concerned in or party to the contravention or failure acted honestly` `it is in the public interest that the order be made` `the person subject to the civil liability concerned acted honestly` `no substantial injustice has been or is likely to be caused to any person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to the following provisions of this section" and subsection (6), "The Court is not to make an order under this section unless it is satisfied"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (5): an order under (4)(a) or (b) may be made although the contravention or failure resulted in an offence.
-- src:27555 | (5) An order may be made under subsection (4)(a) or (b) even
-- src:27556 | though the contravention or failure referred to in the
-- src:27557 | paragraph concerned resulted in the commission of an offence.
@ref s 392(5) (src:27555-27557)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 392(4) kind of order`
      `the contravention or failure resulted in the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(5) the fact that the contravention or failure resulted in an offence does not prevent the order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the contravention or failure resulted in the commission of an offence`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "even though the contravention or failure referred to in the paragraph concerned resulted in the commission of an offence"
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 392(4)(a) an order declaring that an act, matter, thing or proceeding is not invalid by reason of a contravention or failure to comply` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 392(4)(b) an order directing the rectification of a register kept by the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order may be made under subsection (4)(a) or (b)"; the subsection says nothing of an order under (4)(c) or (d)

§ `Section 394: production and inspection of books or papers where an offence is suspected`

DECLARE `s 394(1) kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `s 394(1)(a) an order authorising a person named in it to inspect the books or papers`
    `s 394(1)(b) an order requiring the secretary or another officer named in it to produce the books or papers to a person named in it at a place so named`
    `s 394(1) some other order`

-- src:27593 | 394.—(1) If, on an application made to a judge of the Court in
-- src:27594 | chambers by or on behalf of the Minister, there is shown to be
-- src:27595 | reasonable cause to believe that any person has, while an officer of a
-- src:27596 | company, committed an offence in connection with the management
-- src:27597 | of the company’s affairs and that evidence of the commission of the
-- src:27598 | offence is to be found in any books or papers of or under the control of
-- src:27599 | the company, an order may be made —
-- src:27601 | (a) authorising any person named therein to inspect such
-- src:27602 | books or papers or any of them for the purpose of
-- src:27603 | investigating and obtaining evidence of the offence; or
-- src:27605 | (b) requiring the secretary or such other officer as is named in
-- src:27606 | the order to produce such books or papers or any of them to
-- src:27607 | a person named in the order at a place so named.
@ref s 394(1) (src:27593-27607)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 394(1) kind of order`
      `the application is made to a judge of the Court in chambers by or on behalf of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe that a person has, while an officer of a company, committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `evidence of the commission of the offence is to be found in books or papers of or under the control of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(1) an order of the kind may be made` MEANS
    IF    `the application is made to a judge of the Court in chambers by or on behalf of the Minister`
       AND `there is shown to be reasonable cause to believe that a person has, while an officer of a company, committed an offence in connection with the management of the company's affairs`
       AND `evidence of the commission of the offence is to be found in books or papers of or under the control of the company`
    THEN (CONSIDER kind
          WHEN `s 394(1)(a) an order authorising a person named in it to inspect the books or papers` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 394(1)(b) an order requiring the secretary or another officer named in it to produce the books or papers to a person named in it at a place so named` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "an order may be made (a) ...; or (b) ..." does not say "only"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, on an application ..., there is shown to be reasonable cause ... an order may be made" is an "if" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-394-1)

-- src:27609 | (2) No appeal lies against any order or decision of a judge on or in
-- src:27610 | relation to an application under this section.
@ref s 394(2) (src:27609-27610)
GIVEN `the order or decision is an order or decision of a judge on or in relation to an application under section 394` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(2) an appeal lies against the order or decision` MEANS
    IF `the order or decision is an order or decision of a judge on or in relation to an application under section 394`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No appeal lies against any order or decision of a judge on or in relation to an application under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of an order or decision on an application under section 394

§ `Section 399: the Court may compel compliance`

-- src:27821 | 399.—(1) If any person in contravention of this Act refuses or fails
-- src:27822 | to permit the inspection of any register, minute book or document or
-- src:27823 | to supply a copy of any register, minute book or document the Court
-- src:27824 | may by order compel an immediate inspection of the register, minute
-- src:27825 | book or document or order the copy to be supplied.
@ref s 399(1) (src:27821-27825)
GIVEN `a person in contravention of this Act refuses or fails to permit the inspection of a register, minute book or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person in contravention of this Act refuses or fails to supply a copy of a register, minute book or document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(1) the Court may by order compel an immediate inspection or order the copy to be supplied` MEANS
    IF    `a person in contravention of this Act refuses or fails to permit the inspection of a register, minute book or document`
       OR `a person in contravention of this Act refuses or fails to supply a copy of a register, minute book or document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any person in contravention of this Act refuses or fails ... the Court may" is an "if" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-399-1); the subsection does not say who may apply

-- src:27827 | (2) If any officer or former officer of a company has failed or
-- src:27828 | omitted to do any act, matter or thing which under this Act he or she is
-- src:27833 | or was required or directed to do, the Court on the application of the
-- src:27834 | Registrar or any member of the company or the Official Receiver or
-- src:27835 | liquidator may, by order, require that officer or former officer to do
-- src:27836 | such act, matter or thing immediately or within such time as is
-- src:27837 | allowed by the order, and for the purpose of complying with any such
-- src:27838 | order a former officer is deemed to have the same status, powers and
-- src:27839 | duties as he or she had at the time the act, matter or thing should have
-- src:27840 | been done.
@ref s 399(2) (src:27827-27840)
GIVEN `the officer or former officer of a company has failed or omitted to do an act, matter or thing which under this Act the officer or former officer is or was required or directed to do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Registrar, a member of the company, the Official Receiver or the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(2) the Court may by order require the officer or former officer to do the act, matter or thing immediately or within the time the order allows` MEANS
    IF `the officer or former officer of a company has failed or omitted to do an act, matter or thing which under this Act the officer or former officer is or was required or directed to do` AND `the application is made by the Registrar, a member of the company, the Official Receiver or the liquidator`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any officer or former officer ... has failed ..., the Court on the application of the Registrar or any member of the company or the Official Receiver or liquidator may" is an "if" and "on application" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1; split site type (ii), fork F-399-2)

@ref s 399(2) (src:27827-27840)
GIVEN `the person is a former officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has made an order under section 399(2) for the purpose of complying with which the former officer must act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 399(2) the former officer is deemed to have the same status, powers and duties as at the time the act, matter or thing should have been done` MEANS
    IF `the person is a former officer of the company` AND `the Court has made an order under section 399(2) for the purpose of complying with which the former officer must act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of complying with any such order a former officer is deemed to have the same status, powers and duties"

§ `Section 409A: injunctions`

DECLARE `s 409A(7) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 409A(7) require an undertaking as to damages as a condition of granting an interim injunction`

-- src:28184 | 409A.—(1) Where a person has engaged, is engaging or is
-- src:28185 | proposing to engage in any conduct that constituted, constitutes or
-- src:28186 | would constitute a contravention of this Act, the Court may, on the
-- src:28187 | application of —
-- src:28189 | (a) the Registrar; or
-- src:28191 | (b) any person whose interests have been, are or would be
-- src:28192 | affected by the conduct,
-- src:28194 | grant an injunction restraining the firstmentioned person from
-- src:28195 | engaging in the conduct and, if in the opinion of the Court it is
-- src:28196 | desirable to do so, requiring that person to do any act or thing.
@ref s 409A(1) (src:28184-28196)
GIVEN `the person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage in conduct that constituted, constitutes or would constitute a contravention of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by a person whose interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(1) the Court may grant an injunction restraining the person from engaging in the conduct` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage in conduct that constituted, constitutes or would constitute a contravention of this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage in any conduct that constituted, constitutes or would constitute a contravention of this Act" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-409A-1
    ELSE (IF `the application is made by the Registrar` OR `the application is made by a person whose interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may, on the application of (a) the Registrar; or (b) any person whose interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct" is an "on application" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1; split site type (ii), fork F-409A-1)

-- src:28198 | (2) Where a person has refused or failed, is refusing or failing, or is
-- src:28199 | proposing to refuse or fail, to do an act or thing that the person is
-- src:28200 | required by this Act to do, the Court may, on the application of —
-- src:28202 | (a) the Registrar; or
-- src:28204 | (b) any person whose interests have been, are or would be
-- src:28205 | affected by the refusal or failure to do that act or thing,
-- src:28207 | grant an injunction requiring the firstmentioned person to do that act
-- src:28208 | or thing.
@ref s 409A(2) (src:28198-28208)
GIVEN `the person has refused or failed, is refusing or failing, or is proposing to refuse or fail, to do an act or thing that the person is required by this Act to do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by a person whose interests have been, are or would be affected by the refusal or failure to do that act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(2) the Court may grant an injunction requiring the person to do the act or thing` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has refused or failed, is refusing or failing, or is proposing to refuse or fail, to do an act or thing that the person is required by this Act to do`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person has refused or failed, is refusing or failing, or is proposing to refuse or fail, to do an act or thing that the person is required by this Act to do" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-409A-1
    ELSE (IF `the application is made by the Registrar` OR `the application is made by a person whose interests have been, are or would be affected by the refusal or failure to do that act or thing`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may, on the application of (a) the Registrar; or (b) any person whose interests have been, are or would be affected" (an "on application" gate on a grant; fork F-409A-1)

-- src:28210 | (3) Where an application is made to the Court for an injunction
-- src:28211 | under subsection (1), the Court may, if in the opinion of the Court it is
-- src:28212 | desirable to do so, before considering the application, grant an interim
-- src:28213 | injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct of the kind
-- src:28214 | mentioned in subsection (1) pending the determination of the
-- src:28215 | application.
@ref s 409A(3) (src:28210-28215)
GIVEN `an application is made to the Court for an injunction under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Court it is desirable to grant an interim injunction before considering the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(3) the Court may grant an interim injunction pending the determination of the application` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application is made to the Court for an injunction under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made to the Court for an injunction under subsection (1)" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-409A-3
    ELSE (IF `in the opinion of the Court it is desirable to grant an interim injunction before considering the application`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may, if in the opinion of the Court it is desirable to do so" is an "if" gate on a grant (grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

-- src:28217 | (4) The Court may rescind or vary an injunction granted under
-- src:28218 | subsection (1), (2) or (3).
@ref s 409A(4) (src:28217-28218)
GIVEN `the injunction was granted under subsection (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(4) the Court may rescind or vary the injunction` MEANS
    IF `the injunction was granted under subsection (1), (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an injunction granted under subsection (1), (2) or (3)"

-- src:28220 | (5) Where an application is made to the Court for the grant of an
-- src:28221 | injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct of a
-- src:28222 | particular kind, the power of the Court to grant the injunction may be
-- src:28223 | exercised —
-- src:28228 | (a) if the Court is satisfied that the person has engaged in
-- src:28229 | conduct of that kind — whether or not it appears to the
-- src:28230 | Court that the person intends to engage again, or to
-- src:28231 | continue to engage, in conduct of that kind; or
-- src:28233 | (b) if it appears to the Court that, in the event that an injunction
-- src:28234 | is not granted, it is likely the person will engage in conduct
-- src:28235 | of that kind — whether or not the person has previously
-- src:28236 | engaged in conduct of that kind and whether or not there is
-- src:28237 | an imminent danger of substantial damage to any person if
-- src:28238 | the firstmentioned person engages in conduct of that kind.
@ref s 409A(5) (src:28220-28238)
GIVEN `an application is made to the Court for the grant of an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct of a particular kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the person has engaged in conduct of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court that, in the event that an injunction is not granted, it is likely the person will engage in conduct of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(5) the power of the Court to grant the injunction may be exercised` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application is made to the Court for the grant of an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct of a particular kind`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made to the Court for the grant of an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct of a particular kind" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-409A-5
    ELSE (IF `the Court is satisfied that the person has engaged in conduct of that kind` OR `it appears to the Court that, in the event that an injunction is not granted, it is likely the person will engage in conduct of that kind`
          THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether or not the person intends to engage again, whether or not the person has previously engaged in the conduct, and whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage: none of these is asked
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be exercised (a) if the Court is satisfied ...; or (b) if it appears to the Court" are "if" gates on a grant

-- src:28240 | (6) Where an application is made to the Court for a grant of an
-- src:28241 | injunction requiring a person to do a particular act or thing, the power
-- src:28242 | of the Court to grant the injunction may be exercised —
-- src:28244 | (a) if the Court is satisfied that the person has refused or failed
-- src:28245 | to do that act or thing — whether or not it appears to the
-- src:28246 | Court that the person intends to refuse or fail again, or to
-- src:28247 | continue to refuse or fail, to do that act or thing; or
-- src:28249 | (b) if it appears to the Court that, in the event that an injunction
-- src:28250 | is not granted, it is likely the person will refuse or fail to do
-- src:28251 | that act or thing — whether or not the person has
-- src:28252 | previously refused or failed to do that act or thing and
-- src:28253 | whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial
-- src:28254 | damage to any person if the firstmentioned person refuses
-- src:28255 | or fails to do that act or thing.
@ref s 409A(6) (src:28240-28255)
GIVEN `an application is made to the Court for the grant of an injunction requiring a person to do a particular act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the person has refused or failed to do that act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court that, in the event that an injunction is not granted, it is likely the person will refuse or fail to do that act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(6) the power of the Court to grant the injunction requiring the act or thing may be exercised` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application is made to the Court for the grant of an injunction requiring a person to do a particular act or thing`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made to the Court for a grant of an injunction requiring a person to do a particular act or thing" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-409A-5
    ELSE (IF `the Court is satisfied that the person has refused or failed to do that act or thing` OR `it appears to the Court that, in the event that an injunction is not granted, it is likely the person will refuse or fail to do that act or thing`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be exercised (a) if the Court is satisfied ...; or (b) if it appears to the Court" are "if" gates on a grant

-- src:28257 | (7) Where the Registrar makes an application to the Court for the
-- src:28258 | grant of an injunction under this section, the Court must not require
-- src:28259 | the Registrar or any other person, as a condition of granting an interim
-- src:28260 | injunction, to give any undertakings as to damages.
@ref s 409A(7) (src:28257-28260)
GIVEN `the Registrar makes an application to the Court for the grant of an injunction under section 409A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking as to damages is required as a condition of granting an interim injunction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(7) the Court is barred from requiring the undertaking as to damages` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar makes an application to the Court for the grant of an injunction under section 409A` AND `the undertaking as to damages is required as a condition of granting an interim injunction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the Registrar makes an application ..., the Court must not require the Registrar or any other person, as a condition of granting an interim injunction, to give any undertakings as to damages"; the subsection is silent where the Registrar is not the applicant

@ref s 409A(7) (src:28257-28260)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 409A(7) act`
`s 409A(7) the Court must not require an undertaking as to damages on the Registrar's application` MEANS
    PARTY Court
    SHANT `s 409A(7) require an undertaking as to damages as a condition of granting an interim injunction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Court BECAUSE "the Court required an undertaking as to damages as a condition of granting an interim injunction on the Registrar's application"

-- src:28262 | (8) Where the Court has power under this section to grant an
-- src:28263 | injunction restraining a person from engaging in particular conduct,
-- src:28264 | or requiring a person to do a particular act or thing, the Court may,
-- src:28265 | either in addition to or in substitution for the grant of the injunction,
-- src:28266 | order that person to pay damages to any other person.
@ref s 409A(8) (src:28262-28266)
GIVEN `the Court has power under section 409A to grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in particular conduct, or requiring a person to do a particular act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409A(8) the Court may order the person to pay damages to any other person, in addition to or in substitution for the injunction` MEANS
    IF `the Court has power under section 409A to grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in particular conduct, or requiring a person to do a particular act or thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Court has power under this section to grant an injunction ..." (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); split site type (ii), fork F-409A-8

§ `Section 409C: appeal against the Registrar`

-- src:28340 | (3) This section does not apply to any act or decision of the
-- src:28341 | Registrar —
-- src:28343 | (a) in respect of which any provision in the nature of an appeal
-- src:28344 | or a review is expressly provided in this Act; or
-- src:28346 | (b) which is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final or is
-- src:28347 | embodied in any document declared by this Act to be
-- src:28348 | conclusive evidence of any act, matter or thing.
@ref s 409C(3) (src:28340-28348)
GIVEN `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409C(3) section 409C does not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar` MEANS
    IF    `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision`
       OR `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not apply to any act or decision of the Registrar (a) ...; or (b) ..."; for any other act or decision the subsection is silent

-- (1): "Any party aggrieved by an act or a decision of the Registrar under this Act may, within 28 days after the date of the act or decision, appeal to the Court".
-- The period is counted by sg-periods P2: an appeal on the day of the decision itself is not "within 28 days after" it (fork F-409C-1).
-- src:28328 | 409C.—(1) Any party aggrieved by an act or a decision of the
-- src:28329 | Registrar under this Act may, within 28 days after the date of the act
-- src:28330 | or decision, appeal to the Court against the act or decision.
@ref s 409C(1) (src:28328-28330)
GIVEN `the party is aggrieved by an act or a decision of the Registrar under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the act or decision` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the appeal is brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409C(1) the party may appeal to the Court against the act or decision` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party is aggrieved by an act or a decision of the Registrar under this Act`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any party aggrieved by an act or a decision of the Registrar under this Act may ... appeal"
    ELSE (IF `s 409C(3) section 409C does not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar` `a provision in the nature of an appeal or a review is expressly provided in this Act in respect of the act or decision` `the act or decision is declared by this Act to be conclusive or final, or is embodied in a document declared by this Act to be conclusive evidence of an act, matter or thing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (3), "This section does not apply to any act or decision of the Registrar (a) ...; or (b) ..."
          ELSE (IF `period: the date is within a period after` `the date of the act or decision` `the date on which the appeal is brought` 28 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 28 days after the date of the act or decision" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a): outside the period the answer is JUST FALSE)

-- src:28334 | (2) The Court may confirm the act or decision or give such
-- src:28335 | directions in the matter as seem proper or otherwise determine the
-- src:28336 | matter.
@ref s 409C(2) (src:28334-28336)
GIVEN `an appeal has been brought to the Court under section 409C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409C(2) the Court may confirm the act or decision, give such directions in the matter as seem proper, or otherwise determine the matter` MEANS
    IF `an appeal has been brought to the Court under section 409C(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court's power is its power on the appeal under subsection (1)
